lib/nodal_schureman.rb (NodalSchureman)
Copyright (c) 2026 Jordan Ritter. MIT License; the terms are in the file's
header.

NodalSchureman computes node factors (f) and equilibrium arguments (V0 + u)
for 13 tidal constituents. It is an independent implementation, written from
P. Schureman, "Manual of Harmonic Analysis and Prediction of Tides", U.S. Coast
and Geodetic Survey Special Publication No. 98 (public domain), via a written
functional specification. It was made in a clean-room process: one party wrote
the specification and a test oracle, and a separate party, who did not read
the earlier webcaltides code or any GPL tide code (libcongen, congen or XTide),
wrote the implementation from the specification and SP98 alone. It is not
derived from any other program's source code. See
docs/nodal-cleanroom/PROVENANCE.md.
